  "transcript": "Six months ago, a lot of our work lived in spreadsheets. Estimates priced from memory, store photos nobody could search, AI know-how stuck with a few people. So we stopped working around our tools and built our own. AI-powered apps, live data, and automations. SF Pricing turns a client brief into a good, better, best plan. We trained it on hundreds of our past estimates. It checks with the market charges and drafts a starting point. Our team reviews every number and a person makes the final call. Over $100,000 of work priced so far. Store Walk turns field photos into retail evidence. Every shelf shot gets tagged so anyone can search it in plain English. It drafts a pitch from what we actually saw and our team takes it from there. Every Store Walk searchable in one place. And AI training keeps the whole team current. Our AI team carefully designs each lesson around the tools that matter to each team's work. Lessons land in everyone's quarterly checklist. A learning track for every team. Automations handle the busy work. Hours of SEO work now done in minutes. Same playbook everywhere. Dashboards, pipelines, catalog audits. And we bring the same technical capabilities to our clients, building software for them too. The rule is simple. AI drafts, code does the math, people decide. Behind every app is months of work from our own team. Built by our team, powered by AI, getting smarter every quarter.",
